    "Description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: netfilter: conntrack: remove sprintf usage (CVE-2026-53002)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: synproxy: refresh tcphdr after skb_ensure_writable (CVE-2026-64007)\n\n* kernel: vhost: reset the vring metadata cache on vring reconfiguration (CVE-2026-74580)\n\n* kernel: udp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation (CVE-2026-74705)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* kernel: vhost: reset the vring metadata cache on vring reconfiguration [rhel-7.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-224557)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
